 that the locale count won't change before we close Blocker #1 as 9?\n1. **Sprint-2 content-types table.** Two of these belong in later sprints: SFCC-67 (Checkout Trust Messaging) sits under the Checkout Flow & Delivery epic, which is Sprint 4, and SFCC-14 (Returns/Refund) is an Epic, which is Sprint 7 - and as you and Tim both noted, we build to a child story, not the epic. Let's remove both rows from the Sprint-2 table and relocate them: SFCC-67 under Sprint 4, SFCC-14 under Sprint 7 (attaching to its child story once it's raised).\n\n**Validate Before Finalising**\n\n1. **Sprint-2 content types.** You rightly flagged these are assumed, not confirmed (SFCC-82, SFCC-190, SFCC-67 defer their model to stories not yet created; none map to an HPC requirement in 04.1.1). User:557058:1a7fb05a-783b-4241-a0f1-9a7b046da3a8 - you'd mentioned running the Sprint-2 authoring approach by Emma and Dani; is that still the plan, and how would you like us to sequence it before we lock the field sets? In the meantime, Jhoan, let's mark the Sprint-2 types provisional.\n1. **Mega Menu fields.** Design-dependent, as you noted - SFCC-96 needs the Figma spec first (it's flagged DesignDependent in Jira). Let's mark those fields provisional pending the design.\n\n**Spikes and To-Dos to Raise (Not Blocking)**\n\n1. **PLP Inline Grid Insert.** The ID pattern presents the PLP inject as resolved, but Tim flagged we need to confirm we can inject a Contentful item into the SFCC PLP grid without breaking item counts or pagination. There's already a spike for this area - SFCC-238 (Contentful-to-PWA Kit Product/Category ID Rendering) - let's link it here and confirm it covers the pagination/item-count check, and mark the PLP inject \"pending SFCC-238\" in the meantime.\n1. **PDP Accordion, mixed content.** Tim raised whether the accordion body can pull SFCC content via a simple SFCC var or needs a dedicated component, and you suggested a spike - there's no card for it yet, so let's raise one (or fold it into SFCC-238's scope) and reference it here.\n1. **MRT-apps section.** As agreed, we'll scratch this - the MRT app architecture is covered by its own spike, SFCC-237 (MRT Application Architecture Strategy), which Gideon and I will take; we'll link that TSD here once it's done.\n\n**Raise with Leads / POs (Decisions Outside Our Control)**\n\n1. **Error Handling & Monitoring, New Relic.** Two things: (a) it's currently anchored to the Integration Reconciliation working doc, which is a draft and actually lists New Relic as \"Not Required\", so please re-anchor to the \"CDN, eCDN & Security Configuration\" page (339935324), which references the Accenture Observability, Tracing & Security Assurance deck and holds the Log Centre to New Relic streaming checklist; (b) New Relic isn't procured or on the credentials tracker yet - I've already raised procurement with Emma/IT and we're pending their reply, so let's frame the alert policies as \"recommended, pending procurement.\"\n1. **\"What is NOT in Contentful\", product imagery.** This is asserted as SFCC BM, but it isn't settled: the PWA TSD says imagery is served from Contentful, and the DC002 decision page has no decision recorded yet. User:557058:1a7fb05a-783b-4241-a0f1-9a7b046da3a8 - what's your read on where product imagery lands, and should DC002 be the place we lock it? Jhoan, let's mark it \"pending DC002\" meanwhile rather than stating SFCC BM.\n1. **Cache and graceful degradation.** Since footer and homepage always render from Contentful, a full CDA outage gives a broken bare page, currently noted as \"risk accepted.\" User:557058:1a7fb05a-783b-4241-a0f1-9a7b046da3a8 - you'd raised the cache/invalidation angle here; do you see Contentful as effectively a hard dependency for that chrome, or should we plan a minimal static / last-known-good fallback? Keen on your steer before we lock the degradation stance.\n\n**Minor**\n\n1. **\"Tell No Lies\" link** (Didomi row and monitoring) currently points back to this page - please repoint it to the actual Tell No Lies/GTM reference or drop the hyperlink.\n\nNet: items 1 to 4 are the sign-off blockers (plus the Handoff Boundary table, which Tim already flagged FOR UPDATE to finalise); 5 and 6 need a design/authoring check; 7 to 9 are spikes and to-dos (SFCC-238 and SFCC-237 already exist); 10 to 12 need a lead or PO call - I've raised 10 with Emma/IT, and 11 and 12 are for Tim's steer.\n\nCC: User:5f506d223e9e2e004d7c48ac",
